// Build-mode orchestrator (`tsc -b`). Not extended by anything and does not
// extend tsconfig.base.json itself — it only lists the workspace projects and
// their dependency edges, so `tsc -b` builds/typechecks them in dependency
// order and can resolve @backburner/engine's declarations for
// @backburner/api without a manual build step first. See the "TypeScript
// typecheck strategy" choice called out in the Phase 0 report.
//
// @backburner/web is deliberately ABSENT from this graph. Since Phase 5 it is a
// Vite application: Vite owns the build and its tsconfig is a pure `noEmit`
// checker on bundler resolution, which cannot be a `tsc -b` project reference
// (composite requires emit). Root `npm run typecheck` runs that package's own
// `typecheck` script immediately after this build, so web is still covered.
{
  "files": [],
  "references": [
    { "path": "packages/engine" },
    { "path": "packages/api" },
    { "path": "packages/e2e" }
  ]
}
